 summary="Atrial fibrillation (AF) is disorganised atrial electrical activity with an irregularly irregular ventricular response. Loss of atrial contraction and fast, irregular ventricular rates reduce cardiac output and cause palpitations, breathlessness and fatigue, and can precipitate heart failure or angina. Stasis in the left atrial appendage allows thrombus to form, so stroke prevention with an oral anticoagulant (OAC) is central to care. The ICMR workflow classifies AF as paroxysmal (under 7 days), persistent (7 days to 1 year), long-standing persistent (over 1 year) or permanent (rate control only). Valvular heart disease, including rheumatic mitral stenosis, remains an important cause in India.",
